### 5. How Data Flows Through the Application
1. **User Action**: A user interacts with a page (e.g., Parent clicks "Reserve Slot" on [ReserveQueue.jsx](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/pages/parent/ReserveQueue.jsx)).
2. **Service Layer Invocation**: The component calls a specialized function from `/src/services/` (e.g., `createReservation` in [reservationService.js](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/services/reservationService.js)).
3. **Realtime Database Mutation**: The service pushes or updates data directly in Firebase RTDB (`/reservations`, `/schedules`, `/branchConfigurations`).
4. **Realtime Synchronization (`onValue`)**: Active components across all open clients subscribe to database nodes using service listeners (e.g., `subscribeToAllReservations`, `subscribeToPublishedSchedules`).
5. **State & Eligibility Recalculation**: When RTDB pushes updates, client components re-evaluate dynamic queue ordering and eligibility via [queueEligibilityService.js](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/services/queueEligibilityService.js) (`getNextEligiblePatient`, `calculateDynamicQueuePositions`).
6. **UI Re-render**: The UI seamlessly updates live across Parent, Secretary, and Doctor views without manual page refreshes.

### 6. How Firebase is Integrated
* **Initialization**: Configured in [firebaseConfig.js](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/firebase/firebaseConfig.js) using `initializeApp()`.
* **Authentication**: Exported from [auth.js](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/firebase/auth.js) using `getAuth()`. Managed globally via `onAuthStateChanged` in [AuthContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/context/AuthContext.jsx).
* **Realtime Database**: Exported from [database.js](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/firebase/database.js) using `getDatabase()`. All CRUD operations use Firebase modular functions (`ref`, `get`, `set`, `push`, `update`, `remove`, `onValue`).

### 7. Authentication and Authorization Flow
1. **Authentication**: Users sign in with email/password via Firebase Auth ([loginUser](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/services/authService.js#L43)). New users register via [registerUser](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/services/authService.js#L7), which creates an Auth profile and stores a user document under `users/{uid}` in RTDB with a default role of `"parent"`.
2. **Session Persistence**: [AuthContext.jsx](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/context/AuthContext.jsx) listens for authentication state changes. When authenticated, it queries RTDB (`users/{uid}`) to fetch custom user metadata and the user's assigned role (`parent`, `secretary`, or `doctor`).
3. **Route Guards**:
   * [ProtectedRoute.jsx](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/routes/ProtectedRoute.jsx) blocks unauthenticated users, redirecting them to `/`.
   * [RoleRoute.jsx](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/routes/RoleRoute.jsx) enforces Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). If a user attempts to access a portal outside their role (e.g., a parent navigating to `/doctor`), they are redirected to their assigned portal home.

### 8. Database Structure (Firebase Realtime Database)
The RTDB is structured as a NoSQL JSON tree with four primary root collections:
* `users/{uid}`: Stores user profile information (`uid`, `name`, `email`, `phone`, `role`).
* `branchConfigurations/{branchId}`: Stores clinic branches (`name`, `schedule` object mapped by days of the week containing `isOpen`, `openingTime`, `closingTime`, and timestamp metadata).
* `schedules/{scheduleId}`: Stores doctor clinic sessions (`branch`, `clinicDate`, `startTime`, `endTime`, `slotCapacity`, `status` (`draft` | `published` | `completed`), `queueStatus` (`not_started` | `active` | `paused` | `closed`), `isReady`, timestamps).
* `reservations/{reservationId}`: Stores patient slot bookings (`scheduleId`, `parentId`, `parentName`, `parentEmail`, `childName`, `childAge`, `purpose`, `status` (`reserved` | `waiting` | `checked_in` | `in_consultation` | `consultation_completed` | `cancelled`), `reservationCode` (6-character alphanumeric), `checkedIn` boolean, doctor consultation notes, and timestamps).

