## Phase 5: Technical Debt

1. **Large Monolithic Components (Candidate for Splitting)**:
   * **[Queue.jsx (Doctor)](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/pages/doctor/Queue.jsx)**: Exactly 787 lines (~41 KB). Encapsulates schedule selection, real-time queue data derivation, eligibility checking, consultation start/complete modals, doctor note input, queue state control (pause/close/end), and rendering four distinct patient lists. Should be split into sub-components (`QueueControls`, `PatientQueueList`, `ConsultationModal`, `QueueStatsHeader`).
   * **[MyReservation.jsx (Parent)](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/pages/parent/MyReservation.jsx)**: (~30 KB). Handles tab management, filtering, QR code generation modal, cancellation modal, and detail views in a single file.
   * **[ReserveQueue.jsx (Parent)](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/pages/parent/ReserveQueue.jsx)**: (~26 KB). Combines schedule filtering, date selection, branch operating hour lookups, and booking form submission.
   * **[ValidateReservation.jsx (Secretary)](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/pages/secretary/ValidateReservation.jsx)**: (~20 KB). Combines HTML5 video camera scanning logic, manual text search, and 9 different validation state modals.
2. **Performance & Scalability Concerns**:
   * **Unfiltered Global RTDB Subscriptions**: Functions like `subscribeToAllReservations` ([reservationService.js:L119](file:///c:/Users/canil/OneDrive/Documents/CAPSTONE-PROJECT/pediatric-clinic-queue-system/client/src/services/reservationService.js#L119)) and `subscribeToAllSchedules` attach `onValue` listeners to the **entire root collections** (`/reservations`, `/schedules`). As the clinic operates over months and accumulates thousands of records, downloading the entire database tree to every parent and secretary client on page load will cause severe network bandwidth spikes, memory bloat, and slow rendering. Queries should be indexed and filtered by date or active status (`orderByChild('createdAt')`, `equalTo(...)`).
3. **State Management & Caching Issues**:
   * Multiple independent pages set up identical listeners to `/reservations` and `/schedules` on mount and tear them down on unmount. There is no global state caching layer (such as React Query, SWR, or a global `QueueContext`), resulting in redundant network requests and momentary loading spinners when switching tabs.
4. **Code Smells & Duplicate Logic**:
   * Date and time formatting strings (`toLocaleDateString`, `toLocaleTimeString`) and permanent queue number index calculations are duplicated across `Dashboard.jsx`, `Queue.jsx`, `ManageQueue.jsx`, and `MyReservation.jsx`. These should be extracted into centralized utility helper functions.

